				"⠇⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				182,
				15
			],
			"Message": "feat(mountain-integration): Implement gRPC services for Mountain integration\n\nThis commit establishes the foundation for Cocoon's integration with Mountain by implementing gRPC communication services. The changes enable Cocoon to run as a sidecar process managed by Mountain, following the specifications outlined in MOUNTAIN-COCOON-INTEGRATION.md.\n\nKey additions include:\n- Scripts/cocoon/bootstrap-fork.js: Bootstrap script that initializes Cocoon as a Mountain sidecar process, handling environment setup, service initialization, graceful shutdown, and readiness signaling.\n- Source/Interfaces/IGRPCServerService.ts and Source/Services/GRPCServerService.ts: gRPC server implementation for handling Mountain requests, including request routing, notification handling, and cancellation support with mock implementations for future expansion.\n- Source/Interfaces/IMountainClientService.ts and Source/Services/MountainClientService.ts: gRPC client implementation for communicating with Mountain, supporting connection management, request/notification sending, and error handling.\n- ServiceMapping updates: Registered GRPCServerService and MountainClientService in the dependency injection system for seamless integration with existing services.\n- Documentation: Added comprehensive MOUNTAIN-COCOON-TODO.md with phased implementation TODOs and updated ARCHITECTURE-TODO-CONSOLIDATION.md with Mountain-Cocoon integration priorities.\n- Build script enhancements: Updated Run.sh and prepublishOnly.sh with TODOs for future gRPC protocol compilation and bootstrap script bundling.\n\nThis implementation provides the core infrastructure for bidirectional gRPC communication between Cocoon and Mountain, setting the stage for Phase 1 of the integration. The services include mock routing and protocol handling with detailed TODOs for production-ready features like protocol buffer loading, error recovery, and performance optimization.",
			"SHA": "7879c43f33d2eab86a032dd9bcaa5c7a8d9a8692"
		}
	],
